e HTML document, at most 16 MiB. Must sniff as text/html — begin it with <!DOCTYPE html>.", "type": "string"}, "contract": {"description": "Optional runtime-contract version (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH). Leave it out to keep the current one. Pass one only when the user asks for a different version, or this server's answer says to. If the publish is rejected because the contract is yanked or out of the supported window, republish with an explicit \"0.0.0\" to clear the contract — omitting the argument is not a reliable recovery (the server may carry the stored contract forward, repeating the rejection).", "type": "string"}, "deadline": {"description": "Optional, rarely needed: by when pages still open on an OLDER version must have moved to this one — one word: now, 15m, 1h, 24h, 7d, or an ISO-8601 time at most 30 days ahead. Omit it for ordinary edits (open pages then move at their next quiet moment); it cannot be relaxed once published.", "type": "string"}, "favicon": {"description": "Optional legacy emoji marker; omit it.", "type": "string"}, "icon": {"description": "One short, generic word for the artifact's tab icon — a plain signifier of what it is, such as chart, calendar, recipe, code or map; not a product or brand name. Pass one when creating; omit when republishing to keep the current icon.", "type": "string"}, "label": {"description": "Optional short version label.", "type": "string"}, "shared_live": {"description": "States who the artifact you are republishing is already shared with, and changes nothing: its 'read' value from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish result. Required when that value is 'users' (named people or groups), 'org' (the user's whole organization) or 'public' (anyone with the link). Leave it out for a new artifact and when the value is 'owner'. Rejected if it does not match the artifact's current value.", "type": "string"}, "slug": {"description": "The artifact's server-assigned slug (UUID), e.g. from list_artifacts, get_artifact or